     ],
     "snippet": "Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) is a technique that improves large language model (LLM) responses by fetching relevant facts from an external knowledge base before generating an answer.",
     "snippet_highlighted_words": [
      "a technique that improves large language model (LLM) responses by fetching relevant facts from an external knowledge base before generating an answer"
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "snippet": "How RAG Works",
     "type": "heading"
    },
    {
     "list": [
      {
       "snippet": "Ingestion: Documents, databases, or web pages are split into smaller text chunks and stored as vector embeddings in a vector database."
      },
      {
       "snippet": "Retrieval: When you type a query, the system searches the database for text passages that match the meaning of your question."
      },
      {
       "snippet": "Augmentation: The system combines your original query with the retrieved text facts to create an enriched context prompt."
      },
      {
       "snippet": "Generation: The language model reads the augmented prompt and writes a grounded, accurate response."
      }
     ],
     "type": "list"
    },
    {
     "snippet": "Benefits of RAG",
     "type": "heading"
    },
    {
     "list": [
      {
       "snippet": "Reduces Hallucinations: Grounds the AI in real facts instead of guessing."
      },
      {
       "snippet": "Saves Money: Avoids the high computational cost of retraining or fine-tuning an entire model."
      },
      {
       "snippet": "Uses Private Data: Connects public models to private company documents or recent files without exposing the data."
      }
     ],
     "type": "list"
    },
